## 🗂️ Project Structure

```
src/
  app/
    routes.ts                    // Main route configuration
    react-router.config.ts       // Framework configuration
    routes/
      _layout.tsx               // Root layout
      index.tsx                 // Home route
      about.tsx                 // About route
      users/
        _layout.tsx             // Users layout
        index.tsx               // Users list
        $userId.tsx             // User detail
        $userId.edit.tsx        // User edit
      api/
        users.tsx               // Resource route
  .react-router/
    types/                      // Generated types
```

## 🛣️ Route Configuration

- Use `RouteConfig` type for type-safe route definitions
- Export route array from `app/routes.ts` with `satisfies RouteConfig`
- Use `route()` helper for explicit route definitions
- Use `flatRoutes()` for file-based routing conventions
- Define nested routes with children array
- Use `index()` for default child routes
- Use `layout()` for shared layouts without URL segments

```ts
import {
  type RouteConfig,
  route,
  index,
  layout,
} from "@react-router/dev/routes";

export default [
  index("./routes/index.tsx"),
  route("about", "./routes/about.tsx"),
  layout("./routes/_layout.tsx", [
    route("users", "./routes/users/index.tsx"),
    route("users/:userId", "./routes/users/$userId.tsx"),
  ]),
] satisfies RouteConfig;
```

## 🔒 Type Safety

- Enable type generation with `react-router typegen`
- Import generated types from `./+types/route-name`
- Use `Route.LoaderArgs` and `Route.ActionArgs` for type safety
- Extend `AppLoadContext` interface for custom context
- Use `useRouteLoaderData<typeof loader>()` for cross-route data access
- Configure `rootDirs` in tsconfig for type imports

```ts
import type { Route } from "./+types/user";

export async function loader({ params }: Route.LoaderArgs) {
  // params.userId is typed as string
}

export default function Component({ loaderData }: Route.DefaultProps) {
  // loaderData is fully typed
}
```

## 🧩 Component Structure

- Export `loader`, `action`, and default `Component` from route modules
- Use `Outlet` for rendering nested routes
- Create layout components for shared UI
- Handle loading states with `HydrateFallback`
- Implement error boundaries with `ErrorBoundary`
- Use `shouldRevalidate` for optimization control

```tsx
import { Outlet } from "react-router-dom";

export default function Layout() {
  return (
    <div>
      <nav>Navigation</nav>
      <main>
        <Outlet />
      </main>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## 📊 Data Loading

- Use `loader` for data fetching and preparation
- Use `action` for form submissions and mutations
- Return `Response` objects for resource routes
- Use `redirect()` for navigation after actions
- Implement `shouldRevalidate` for cache control
- Use `useLoaderData()` and `useActionData()` hooks

```ts
export async function loader({ params }: Route.LoaderArgs) {
  const user = await getUser(params.userId);
  if (!user) throw new Response("Not found", { status: 404 });
  return { user };
}

export async function action({ request }: Route.ActionArgs) {
  const formData = await request.formData();
  await updateUser(formData);
  return redirect("/users");
}
```

## ⚡ Performance Optimization

- Enable SSR with `ssr: true` in config
- Configure pre-rendering with `prerender` array
- Use `lazy` imports for code splitting
- Implement `dataStrategy` for custom data fetching
- Use presets for bundle optimization
- Configure `serverBundles` for server-side code splitting

```ts
// react-router.config.ts
export default {
  ssr: true,
  async prerender() {
    return ["/", "/about", "/contact"];
  },
} satisfies Config;
```

## 🔧 Vite Integration

- Use `@react-router/dev/vite` plugin instead of React plugin
- Configure `react-router.config.ts` for framework settings
- Enable type generation with Vite plugin
- Use `@react-router/node` for SSR runtime
- Configure `rootDirs` in tsconfig for generated types
- Use `--watch` flag for development type generation

```ts
// vite.config.ts
import { reactRouter } from "@react-router/dev/vite";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [reactRouter()],
});
```

## 🎯 Route Patterns

- Use `:param` for dynamic segments
- Use `:param?` for optional segments
- Use `*` for catch-all routes
- Use `/*` for splat routes
- Use `edit?` for optional static segments
- Group routes with `prefix()` helper

```ts
route("users/:userId/edit?", "./routes/users/$userId.tsx"), // Optional edit
route("files/*", "./routes/files.tsx"),                    // Splat route
route(":lang?/categories", "./routes/categories.tsx"),     // Optional lang
```

## 🔄 Resource Routes

- Create routes without default component export
- Return `Response` objects from loaders/actions
- Handle multiple HTTP methods in single route
- Use `reloadDocument` prop for external links
- Set appropriate content-type headers
- Implement proper error handling

```tsx
export async function loader({ params }: Route.LoaderArgs) {
  const pdf = await generatePDF(params.id);
  return new Response(pdf, {
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/pdf" },
  });
}
```

## 🎨 Component Routes

- Use `Routes` and `Route` for component-based routing
- Define routes within components for dynamic routing
- Use `createRoutesFromElements` for JSX route definitions
- Implement wizard flows and multi-step forms
- Handle conditional routing based on state

```tsx
import { Routes, Route } from "react-router-dom";

function Wizard() {
  return (
    <Routes>
      <Route index element={<StepOne />} />
      <Route path="step-2" element={<StepTwo />} />
      <Route path="step-3" element={<StepThree />} />
    </Routes>
  );
}
```

## 🛡️ Error Handling

- Implement error boundaries for route errors
- Use `ErrorBoundary` export for custom error UI
- Handle 404 errors with catch-all routes
- Return proper HTTP status codes
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Log errors appropriately

```tsx
export function ErrorBoundary() {
  return <div>Something went wrong</div>;
}

export async function loader() {
  throw new Response("Not found", { status: 404 });
}
```
